Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] kbase: prepare transactional GPU fence waits

Purpose: Inactive per-queue FENCE_WAIT/SET payload/SET done bridge, CLOEXEC snapshot, transactional PanVK staging, guarded CALL, error-checking completion and checked teardown; no series selection or runtime qualification.
Source/Reference: https://github.com/NothingOSS/android_kernel_modules_nothing_mt6878/tree/5f75a3b13e8135d45b4b0b70ec893345144f70df; locally supplied mali-r44p1 CSF UAPI and KCPU source.
Tested GPU: NOT EXECUTED; intended Moto G86 Mali-G615 MC2, PAN_ARCH 11.
Tested Kbase UAPI: Host layout/command mocks only; intended CSF 1.21 (mali-r44p1).
Mesa base range: 13baeb70c066a9f82d2bcfb29f06e4865212affa with g615-v11-csf prerequisites.
Dependencies: Complete default g615-v11-csf series including sync 002-005; requires gate 1.3 publication/termination evidence, ABI builds and separately approved selection before use.
Validation test: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_kbase_gpu_fence_wait.py

Status: DRAFT, inactive and unqualified. This patch is not selected by any build.
PANVK_KBASE_GPU_FENCE_WAITS defaults to false even in a prepared candidate.
Host mocks do not prove cross-cell CPU/GPU ordering, kernel consumer termination,
Android/glibc linkage or firmware behavior. DELETE requires already-terminated
CSF consumers; failed CSF teardown or DELETE retains queue resources and event BO.
OK means three accepted commands, not successful fence completion.

